{"schemaVersion":1,"albumId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a","editionNumber":1,"candidateContentHash":"398a5b7d10a8a5cbaa7cc3a68e56655a97b8b30bf685078e2aacdbf15c16b4af","reviewer":{"identity":"codex-independent-evidence-reviewer","runId":"rank19-final-readonly-review-20260903","process":"codex exec --sandbox read-only"},"reviewedAt":"2026-09-03T16:11:53Z","decisions":[{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:1:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:1:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact exists, the canonical URL matches the sourceRef URL, and the retainedText slice exactly matches the extract. The extract directly states that the opening track \"Wesley's Theory\" refers to Wesley Snipes and his tax-evasion imprisonment, so it supports the track-specific claim."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:2:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:2:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact exists, URL binding matches, and the character-offset slice exactly matches the extract. The extract explicitly names \"For Free? (Interlude)\" and describes Lamar's dense spoken-word-esque rapping with Robert Glasper's musical accompaniment."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:3:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:3:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The referenced artifact exists, the sourceRef URL matches its canonical URL, and the extract is an exact retainedText slice. The extract directly states that \"King Kunta\" is concerned with the quoted history of negative stereotypes."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:4:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:4:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact exists, canonical/sourceRef URLs match, and the character-offset slice exactly equals the extract. The extract explicitly states Bilal features on \"Institutionalized\" and \"These Walls\" and provides the listed uncredited backing vocals, supporting the full claim for this track."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:5:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:5:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact is present, URL binding is correct, and the slice exactly matches the retained extract. The extract names \"These Walls\" and gives the Billboard description quoted in the candidate claim."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:6:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:6:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The referenced artifact exists, its canonical URL matches the sourceRef, and the section offsets produce the exact extract. The extract directly states that Lamar revealed \"U\" was inspired by his depression and suicidal thoughts."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:7:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:7:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact exists, the URL binding matches, and the retainedText slice exactly equals the sourceRef extract. The extract specifically names \"Alright\" and contains the full spoken-word, jazz horns, drum beats, rapping, troubles, and temptations description in the claim."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:8:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:8:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact exists, canonical/sourceRef URLs match, and the exact retainedText slice matches the extract. The extract states that Lotus produced a discarded version of \"For Sale? (Interlude)\" and that Lamar used Taz Arnold's version; the immediately preceding retainedText identifies Lotus as producer Flying Lotus."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:9:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:9:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact is present, its canonical URL matches the sourceRef URL, and the offset slice exactly matches the extract. The extract directly states that the instrumental of \"Momma\" was originally released as \"So[Rt]\" by Knxwledge."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:10:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:10:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The referenced artifact exists, URL binding is correct, and the character-offset slice exactly equals the extract. The extract specifically says \"Hood Politics\" contains a sample of \"All for Myself\", written and performed by Sufjan Stevens."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:11:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:11:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact exists, the canonical URL matches the sourceRef, and the retainedText slice exactly matches the extract. The extract says Isley performed on \"How Much a Dollar Cost\" with James Fauntleroy, and the immediately preceding retainedText identifies him as Ronald Isley."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:12:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:12:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The artifact exists, sourceRef and canonical URLs match, and the offsets slice the retainedText to the exact extract. The extract directly states that Rapsody appeared on the album and contributed a verse to \"Complexion (A Zulu Love)\"."},{"claimId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:13:fact-1","decisionId":"019-kendrick-lamar-to-pimp-a-butterfly-0dd5449a:1:13:fact-1","decision":"supported","artifactIds":["027972335dbbd4c66e1234b4746a5c261b4fbcc2aba80dd0d8095a76f2da764a"],"sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Pimp_a_Butterfly"],"rationale":"The referenced artifact is present, the canonical URL matches, and the retainedText slice exactly equals the extract. The extract names \"The Blacker the Berry\"